WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.092
Top N per group is a common CTE plus window pattern.

00:00:05.092 --> 00:00:08.557
First calculate a rank inside each group.

00:00:08.557 --> 00:00:12.092
Then put that ranked result in a CTE.

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:15.902
Finally filter the rank in the outer query.

00:00:15.902 --> 00:00:22.462
The separation is useful because window functions are computed before the outer filtering stage.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:25.112
GROUP BY collapses rows; PARTITION BY does not.

00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:33.912
That distinction lets you compute group totals, percentages, or rankings while preserving detail.

00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:40.142
For top-N-per-group problems, rank within each group first and then filter the ranked result in an outer

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:41.200
query.
